From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:52:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] BD-J: read the XML of a disc by itself (no external entities,
 DTDs or XInclude)

libbluray parses two XML files that come from a disc: the manifest of a disc update (BUMFParser,
from VFSManager.requestUpdating()) and the font index of AUXDATA (FontIndex). Both took a SAX
parser with the defaults, which read every external DTD and entity a file names: from the
network, or a file of the system (XXE). Measured on the build host with the parsers before this
change: a manifest with an external entity to a URL, a parameter entity, or a DTD on
the network connected to it; one with an entity to a file opened that file (a FIFO there: the
parser blocked); FontIndex resolved the DVB DTD to nothing but fetched any other.

SafeXML gives both one parser: secure processing on (the parser's limits; a "billion laughs"
stops at once), external general and parameter entities off, the external DTD not loaded,
XInclude off, no protocol allowed for an external DTD or schema, and a file that declares an
external entity is not read at all (a reference to an external parameter entity, skipped, would
not stop it otherwise). Any entity the parser still asks for is an empty document, never the
network or a file, and an entity that was not read ends the parsing. A parser that does not know
one of these settings is not used: the caller reads nothing.

Valid files read as before: the same assets of a manifest, the same fonts of a font index with
the DTD of DVB-MHP, which the parser does not need (it does not validate). A manifest or font
index that names a DTD on the network now reads without fetching it; before, it failed where
that DTD could not be fetched.
---
 .../bdj/java/org/videolan/BUMFParser.java     |  13 +-
 .../bdj/java/org/videolan/FontIndex.java      |  17 +--
 .../bdj/java/org/videolan/SafeXML.java        | 114 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 134 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/SafeXML.java

diff --git a/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/BUMFParser.java b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/BUMFParser.java
index 76ff073..fc65e4d 100644
--- a/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/BUMFParser.java
+++ b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/BUMFParser.java
@@ -24,8 +24,8 @@ import java.io.IOException;
 import java.util.LinkedList;
 
 import javax.xml.parsers.SAXParser;
-import javax.xml.parsers.SAXParserFactory;
 import org.xml.sax.Attributes;
+import org.xml.sax.InputSource;
 import org.xml.sax.SAXException;
 import org.xml.sax.helpers.DefaultHandler;
 
@@ -52,7 +52,8 @@ public class BUMFParser extends DefaultHandler {
         FileInputStream stream = null;
         try {
             stream = new FileInputStream(manifestFile);
-            SAXParser parser = SAXParserFactory.newInstance().newSAXParser();
+            /* the manifest by itself: nothing it names outside the file is read (SafeXML) */
+            SAXParser parser = SafeXML.newParser();
             parser.parse(stream, this);
         } catch (Exception e) {
             logger.error("Binding unit manifest file parsing failed: " + e);
@@ -69,6 +70,14 @@ public class BUMFParser extends DefaultHandler {
 
     private LinkedList assets = new LinkedList();
 
+    public InputSource resolveEntity(String publicId, String systemId) {
+        return SafeXML.noEntity(publicId, systemId);
+    }
+
+    public void skippedEntity(String name) throws SAXException {
+        SafeXML.skipped(name);
+    }
+
     /*
      *
